// Package config loads and validates this service's configuration, and is
// the ONLY package in this service that may read an environment variable.
//
// That rule is what makes `make config` able to print the effective
// configuration truthfully. One os.Getenv somewhere else and the printed
// configuration is no longer the configuration the service is running on.
//
// Belongs here: the config struct, its defaults, YAML loading, environment
// overlay, validation at startup, and the masked rendering used by
// `make config`.
//
// Does NOT belong here: anything that *uses* a config value. Configuration is
// read once at startup and passed down as arguments; packages do not reach
// back up for it.
//
// Precedence is environment variables over YAML, with deliberately no third
// source. See docs/config.md.
//
// The files: config.go is the config type, the reflective walk that derives
// every environment variable name from it, and the loader; source.go is the
// ordered source list and the only read of os.Environ in this service;
// duration.go is the one type whose textual form both languages must agree
// on; render.go is `make config`.
package config
